  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Colombian-Caribbean accordion-led song-form codified 1940s-onward in Valledupar (Cesar-department, northeastern Colombia) from earlier 19th-century rural-troubadour traditions of the Magdalena-basin cattle-ranch lineage. The canonical ensemble: button-accordion (the diatonic Hohner-3-row accordion imported via 1880s-onward German maritime-trade with Caribbean-port-cities), caja-vallenata small two-headed drum, guacharaca grooved-bamboo scraper. The four canonical vallenato airs: paseo moderate-tempo-narrative, merengue (different from Dominican) faster-2/4, son slower-double-meter, and puya fastest-rural-virtuosic. The lyric-tradition is heavily narrative-storytelling, often improvised, and the Vallenato-Festival-de-la-Leyenda annual competition (since 1968) codifies regional standards.",
